        "Excellent <strong>response time</strong> and completely fair — no starvation ever.",
        "Average turnaround time is usually <strong>worse</strong> than SJF.",
        "If the quantum is <strong>very large</strong>, RR becomes exactly FCFS.",
        "If the quantum is <strong>very small</strong>, response is great but context-switch overhead destroys performance (this extreme is called processor sharing).",
        "Rule of thumb: choose a quantum such that about 80% of CPU bursts finish within one quantum."
