      "explain": "A <strong>Multilevel Queue</strong> splits the ready queue into several fixed queues with different priorities. A <strong>Multilevel Feedback Queue (MLFQ)</strong> goes one step further and lets a process <em>move between</em> queues based on its behaviour: a process that uses up its whole quantum is demoted to a lower-priority queue, while one that waits too long is promoted. This way the OS discovers which processes are interactive and which are CPU-hungry, without being told.",
